Litoral-Void

Creative Catalyst: The genre was born when the crew of the Icarus-V generation ship repurposed their navigation array to translate cosmic radiation into Tropicalia melodies during the long drift to Proxima Centauri.

This sound is an impossible hydro-acoustic hallucination: the frantic, syncopated strumming of Bahia transposed onto the cold, crystalline geometry of space. It sounds like an orchestra of wet glass shattering inside a vacuum, held together by the buttery, warm analog grit of a Prophet-5 playing chords that move in non-Euclidean intervals. It is buoyant, airy, and deeply disorienting—a tropical beach vacation occurring on a dead moon, where the waves are made of liquid helium.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 122–128 BPM; a "stutter-skitter" shuffle that mimics a heartbeat under G-force pressure.
*   Harmonic Palette: Lydian-Dominant modes flavored with bit-crushed polytonal clusters; heavy emphasis on high-frequency "sheen" over sub-bass foundations.
*   Production Signatures: "Cryo-Glitch" (injecting liquid-nitrogen hisses into the snare transients), "Orbital Filtering" (applying LFOs that move in time with artificial day/night cycles), and "Tape-Saturating the Vacuum" (simulating analog hiss in spaces where sound shouldn't travel).
*   Dynamics: Startlingly brittle peaks that collapse into expansive, breathy "decompression" breakdowns.

Scene & Origin Lore
The Icarus-V settlers, suffering from "deep-well lethargy," developed a subculture known as Sideral-Samba. Forbidden from using traditional drums due to hull-vibration risks, they invented "Piezo-Percussion," tapping the hull's internal structural spars with electromagnetic rings. Their fashion mimics deep-sea bioluminescence—transparent, vacuum-sealed polymer suits filled with flickering neon gases and hand-woven vines harvested from the ship's hydroponics bay. A core ritual, the Mid-Transit Wake, involves tuning every Prophet-5 on board to a specific star-chart frequency, resulting in a wall of sound so intense it is said to temporarily liquefy the ship's internal lighting.

Central Instruments: Sequential Circuits Prophet-5 (the heart of the melodic drift), glass-encased steel pans, piezoelectric hull-strut triggers, and vocoders modeled after bird calls of the long-lost Amazon basin.

