- Story & Context: Kaelen, the ship’s primary sound-weaver, wept while performing this piece to soothe the infants in the stasis-dormitories, his tears drifting in perfect spheres around the keyboard. He recalled his grandmother's porch in Salvador before the evacuation, the memory manifesting as a concrete phantom of a salt-crusted wooden gate appearing in the corridor. "Only the salt knows the shape of the ghost," he hummed, his voice layered in unnatural harmonies.
