Track 3: The Tide Recedes to Nowhere
- Story & Context: Centuries later, the Icarus-V arrived at a barren rock, and the crew held a funeral for the ship itself by ejecting the core navigation Prophet-5 into the freezing Proxima dust. As the unit hit the ground, it played one final, dissonant chord that echoed across the entire valley, permanently staining the local geography with a permanent, humming vibration. The legend of the "Singing Stone" keeps the survivors awake, whispering, "The current has finished its work," even though the planet remains entirely empty.
